    "already_answered": "partly",
    "cited": ["FAM:SF-APPS-067", "FAM:SF-APPM-022", "FAM:SF-APPA-050"],
    "summary": "Prior work studied the opposite direction (opponent play type → your next-possession PPP) and found sparse, small effects after rigorous matching. Star-suppression studies suggested individual play types can matter but lacked multiplicity control and adequate sample sizes. The direct question of whether your play type influences the opponent's next-possession PPP, and whether own-sequence lags matter, has not been tested."
