    "estimand": "Average treatment effect of own team's play type X on the opponent's points per possession in the immediately following defensive possession, relative to the expected opponent PPP given the defensive matchup and game state, conditional on X being clearly identified.",
    "unit": "A linked pair of possessions: (i) an offensive possession by Team A that ended with a play type X assignment; (ii) the immediately following defensive possession for Team A, which is the opponent's offensive possession.",
    "sample": "All regular season and playoff possessions from the 2022-23 through 2025-26 NBA seasons, excluding garbage time (lead ≥20 in last 5 minutes of the 4th quarter) and possessions with unclear play-type labeling (e.g., transition ambiguous). Use the complete 2025-26 season once available; the partial season up to 2026-06-19 is used for initial exploration.",
    "power": "Set minimum detectable effect size at -0.06 PPP (comparable to SF-APPS-067 findings). For play types occurring at least 800 times per season (~30 per team), a four-season sample yields >3000 observations, providing >80% power at α=0.05 (two-sided) assuming a PPP standard deviation of 1.3. Simulation-based power analysis will be pre-registered with the exact observed frequency distribution.",
    "controls": "Primary: match each possession with play type X to a counterfactual possession by the same defensive team (Team A) on the same date, with similar score margin (±3), period, and opponent offensive rating (±2 pts/100), but where Team A ran a different play type. Sensitivity: regression adjustment with defensive-team fixed effects, opponent offensive rating linear term, previous-made indicator, and home/away indicator.",
    "falsification": "1) Placebo forward: use the opponent's possession *after* the next (i.e., two possessions later) as outcome; any effect there indicates temporal confounding. 2) Permutation test: randomly shuffle play-type labels within each team-game and re-estimate the effect distribution; the true effect should lie outside the null distribution. 3) Check that effects vanish when defensive-team quality is not matched. 4) Out-of-sample validation: estimate the effect in even seasons (2022-23 + 2024-25) and test on odd seasons (2023-24 + 2025-26); report consistency.",
    "multiplicity": "Pre-register a primary set of 8 most frequent play types (ISOLATION, PNR_BALL_HANDLER, PNR_ROLL_MAN, SPOT_UP, TRANSITION, POST_UP, CUT, OFF_SCREEN). All 8 main effects are tested with Benjamini-Hochberg FDR control at q=0.1. Any exploratory extensions (e.g., own-sequence lags) will be reported as secondary with Bonferroni-Holm over the total number of secondary tests.",
    "decision_rule": "A play type is considered for AVOID labeling only if: (a) its estimated opponent-PPP delta is < -0.05 PPP (worse for defense) or > +0.05 PPP (better), (b) the FDR-adjusted p-value < 0.1, (c) the effect replicates in the out-of-sample holdout, and (d) it passes all falsification tests. Otherwise, the conclusion is that opponent next-possession PPP does not provide sufficient signal for AVOID labels for the tested play types.",
    "data_version": "NBA Stats API per-game play-by-play and derived play-type possessions as of 2026-06-19, with reproducible data pull scripts that include versioned schema of the graph database. All data processing steps (possession linking, play-type extraction, matching) will be containerised."
  }
}}

